ellow",[96],[1813,1814],{"_52":346,"_27":347},{"_52":96,"_27":97},[1816],{"_52":1817,"_27":1818,"_247":1819},"Read the explicit Claude Code credit","https://github.com/aebrer/deep-yellow/blob/master/CREDITS.md#code-and-design","Creator attribution specifically names Claude via Claude Code. The itch page separately discloses AI assistance for code; no complete session transcript is supplied.",[1821],{"_52":1822,"_27":1823,"_247":1824},"Open the complete Godot game","https://github.com/aebrer/deep-yellow","Full Godot 4.6 project, scenes, scripts, assets, shaders, and export presets. The itch page lists code MIT and assets CC0, while CREDITS.md still leaves the original-code license undecided and some third-party licenses unspecified; inspect both before reuse.",[1826],{"_52":364,"_27":1827,"_247":1828},"https://github.com/aebrer/deep-yellow/releases/tag/v0.13.0","Download — Prepared Windows and Linux builds, plus a self-hostable Web export. These are uploaded game builds, separate from automatic source archives. Release files were verified; native builds were not executed.",[1830],{"_52":1831,"_27":1810,"_247":1832},"Play DEEP YELLOW","In-development browser build plus Windows/Linux downloads. The creator recommends Chrome or a controller; Firefox mouse input has known problems. Includes horror themes and an interactive tutorial.",[1834],{"_52":1835,"_27":1810,"_247":-7},"Read the creator’s game and development notes",[1837,1838,1839,1840],"Play the interactive tutorial and compare moving, waiting, equipment, and sanity.","Read the creator’s AI disclosure and the project’s separate attribution file.","Import project.godot in Godot 4.6 and inspect the start menu, procedural levels, and turn systems.","Change one equipment or turn rule, then test a complete run and restart.","Drew Brereton identifies the game as code-assisted by Claude. The project credits specifically name Claude Code and distinguish original work from external shaders, textures, and fonts.","Godot 4.6 · GDScript",[1837,1838,1839,1840],{"_52":1835,"_27":1810,"_19":302},{"_52":1831,"_27":1810,"_19":258,"_247":1832},{"_52":1822,"_27":1823,"_300":301,"_247":1824},{"_52":1817,"_27":1818,"_247":1819},[381,118],[1850],{"_866":364,"_27":1827,"_19":358,"_247":1851},"Prepared Windows and Linux builds, plus a self-hostable Web export. These are uploaded game builds, separate from automatic source archives. Release files were verified; native builds were not executed.","example:pelican-bike-claude","pelican-bike-claude","Pelican on a Bike","Ride a helmeted pelican along a procedural coast, change lanes to catch fish, jump and unlock small achievements. The complete Three.js project includes its own character, bicycle, ocean, audio and day/night systems.","/examples/pelican-bike-claude/",{"_21":1853,"_23":1854,"_25":1855,"_108":157,"_90":113,"_287":292,"_284":1906,"_9":1907,"_268":1908,"_20":1909,"_34":1910,"_243":1911,"_236":1912},[1859,1860,1861,1862,1863,1864,1865,1866,1867,1868,1869,1870,1871,1872,1873,1874,1875,1876,1877],{"_50":23,"_54":1854,"_56":23,"_58":-7},{"_50":112,"_54":1855,"_56":25,"_58":-7},{"_50":51,"_52":289,"_54":157,"_56":108,"_58":59},{"_50":51,"_52":88,"_54":89,"_56":90,"_58":91},{"_50":51,"_52":285,"_54":286,"_56":287,"_58":87},{"_50":51,"_52":282,"_54":1906,"_56":284,"_58":59},{"_50":229,"_52":274,"_275":276,"_62":1901,"_56":9,"_58":-7},{"_50":60,"_52":269,"_62":1898,"_56":268,"_58":-7},{"_50":51,"_52":266,"_54":847,"_56":268,"_58":-7},{"_50":51,"_52":264,"_54":265,"_56":20,"_58":-7},{"_50":60,"_52":259,"_62":1894,"_56":20,"_58":-7},{"_50":51,"_52":257,"_54":258,"_56":20,"_58":-7},{"_50":60,"_52":251,"_62":1890,"_56":34,"_58":-7},{"_50":51,"_52":249,"_54":250,"_56":34,"_58":-7},{"_50":60,"_52":241,"_62":1886,"_56":243,"_58":-7},{"_50":60,"_52":234,"_62":1883,"_56":236,"_58":-7},{"_50":229,"_56":230,"_52":231,"_62":1882},{"_50":219,"_56":116,"_52":1878,"_73":1879,"_83":1880,"_34":1881,"_224":225,"_226":227,"_57":228},{"_50":51,"_56":216,"_52":217,"_54":1468},"The live coastal ride after acceleration, a first jump and a camera change.","/GameMap/media/learning/pelican-bike-claude.webp","A white pelican riding a bicycle along a three-dimensional coast, with speed, distance, fish and achievement HUD.","https://claude-opus-5-5.riba2534.cn/",[96],[1884,1885],{"_52":96,"_27":97},{"_52":691,"_27":692},[1887],{"_52":1548,"_27":1888,"_247":1889},"https://github.com/riba2534/claude-opus-5-5-demo#readme","Creator-published prompt and session summary, with exact Claude Code attribution. The model-led long-run tests described there were not repeated by GameMap.",[1891],{"_52":355,"_27":1892,"_247":1893},"https://github.com/riba2534/claude-opus-5-5-demo/tree/main/pelican-bike","Complete pelican-bike source, build script and procedural assets. Run npm install and node build.mjs in that subdirectory, then open dist/index.html. The repository contains three distinct games; this case selects only the pelican game. Package metadata names ISC, but no repository-wide licence text is supplied.",[1895],{"_52":1896,"_27":1881,"_247":1897},"Play Pelican on a Bike","Keyboard and touch controls; W/S accelerate/brake, A/D change lanes, Space jumps and C changes camera. A muted entry is available. Desktop launch, acceleration, jump achievement and camera change were checked.",[1899],{"_52":1900,"_27":1888,"_247":-7},"Read the original prompt and development account",[1902,1903,1904,1905],"Start a muted ride, accelerate with W/S, change lanes with A/D and jump with Space.","Compare the published one-sentence prompt with the pelican, bicycle, cloth, ocean and camera modules.","In pelican-bike, install dependencies and run node build.mjs; open the resulting dist/index.html in a browser.","Change one collection or cycling rule, then check movement, jump, score feedback and restart.","The creator reports generating the game with Claude Opus 5.5 in Claude Code from one Chinese sentence. The README publishes that prompt and describes model-led browser testing and later fixes; the no-manual-code claim is the creator’s, not a measured authorship audit.",[1902,1903,1904,1905],{"_52":1900,"_27":1888,"_19":847},{"_52":1896,"_27":1881,"_19":258,"_247":1897},{"_52":355,"_27":1892,"_300":301,"_247":1893},{"_52":1548,"_27":1888,"_247":1889},[118,722],"example:minimal-rogue-claude","minimal-rogue-claude","Minimal Rogue","Explore a monochrome dungeon, break blocks, manage stamina and equipment, and descend through an ASCII-style roguelike with English and Japanese interfaces.","/examples/minimal-rogue-claude/",{"_21":1914,"_23":1915,"_25":1916,"_108":1967,"_90":291,"_287":515,"_284":1966,"_9":1968,"_268":1969,"_20":1970,"_34":1971,"_243":1972,"_236":1973},[1920,1921,1922,1923,1924,1925,1926,1927,1928,1929,1930,1931,1932,1933,1934,1935,1936,1937,1938],{"_50":23,"_54":1915,"_56":23,"_58":-7},{"_50":112,"_54":1916,"_56":25,"_58":-7},{"_50":51,"_52":289,"_54":1967,"_56":108,"_58":59},{"_50":51,"_52":88,"_54":288,"_56":90,"_58":91},{"_50":51,"_52":285,"_54":513,"_56":287,"_58":87},{"_50":51,"_52":282,"_54":1966,"_56":284,"_58":59},{"_50":229,"_52":274,"_275":276,"_62":1961,"_56":9,"_58":-7},{"_50":60,"_52":269,"_62":1958,"_56":268,"_58":-7},{"_50":51,"_52":266,"_54":436,"_56":268,"_58":-7},{"_50":51,"_52":264,"_54":1626,"_56":20,"_58":-7},{"_50":60,"_52":259,"_62":1954,"_56":20,"_58":-7},{"_50":51,"_52":257,"_54":258,"_56":20,"_58":-7},{"_50":60,"_52":251,"_62":1950,"_56":34,"_58":-7},{"_50":51,"_52":249,"_54":250,"_56":34,"_58":-7},{"_50":60,"_52":241,"_62":1946,"_56":243,"_58":-7},{"_50":60,"_52":234,"_62":1944,"_56":236,"_58":-7},{"_50":229,"_56":230,"_52":231,"_62":1943},{"_50":219,"_56":116,"_52":1939,"_73":1940,"_83":1941,"_34":1942,"_224":225,"_226":227,"_57":228},{"_50":51,"_56":216,"_52":217,"_54":1468},"The live first-floor room after normal movement and block-cracking inputs.","/GameMap/media/learning/minimal-rogue-claude.webp","Minimal Rogue first-floor gameplay with the player, breakable blocks, corridor, HP and stamina HUD, and block-cracking log.","https://hirotaka-adachi.itch.io/minimal-rogue",[96],[1945],{"_52":96,"_27":97},[1947],{"_52":1948,"_27":1942,"_247":1949},"Read the author’s Claude Code and SUNO attribution","The creator identifies Claude Code for development, SUNO AI for music, links the complete repository and explicitly describes the work as created entirely using AI. No model version or full development transcript is supplied.",[1951],{"_52":355,"_27":1952,"_247":1953},"https://github.com/HirotakaAdachi/Rogue/tree/anonymous-release","Complete static HTML/CSS/JavaScript project and four MP3 tracks; serve the root over HTTP without a package install or build step. MIT code license is included; SUNO music is credited without a separate music license. The reviewed public source index references script version 549, while the itch build references 581, so the two releases are not claimed to be byte-identical.",[1955],{"_52":1956,"_27":1942,"_247":1957},"Play Minimal Rogue on itch.io","Browser keyboard game. Enter confirms the opening and tutorial; arrows move, Space defends, and X opens the menu. A short first-floor run verified movement, block-cracking feedback and the command menu. Later floors, saves and a complete run were not tested.",[1959],{"_52":1960,"_27":1942,"_247":-7},"Read the creator’s AI and source-code notes",[1962,1963,1964,1965],"Run the browser game, choose a new game and language, and confirm the opening and tutorial with Enter.","Use the arrow keys to explore the first room, Space to defend and X to open the command menu.","Read the creator’s AI disclosure and inspect the complete HTML, CSS, JavaScript and music files.","Serve the source folder over HTTP, change one room or stamina rule, and check movement, interactions and a new run.","Hirotaka Adachi names Claude Code as the development tool and SUNO AI for music, and describes the work as entirely AI-created. The exact coding model is not identified. The public project contains the game renderer, rules, interface and four music files; the creator’s claim does not establish autonomous development without human direction.","Canvas 2D · Vanilla JavaScript · HTML/CSS UI",[1962,1963,1964,1965],{"_52":1960,"_27":1942,"_19":436},{"_52":1956,"_27":1942,"_19":258,"_247":1957},{"_52":355,"_27":1952,"_300":301,"_247":1953},{"_52":1948,"_27":1942,"_247":1949},[118],"example:polar-icecapade-claude","polar-icecapade-claude","Polar Icecapade","Slide across icy 3D arenas, use a three-hit melee combo to propel yourself forward, and fire projectiles that push you backward. Open gates and collect coins while confronting a rat regime in a short game-jam adventure.","/examples/polar-icecapade-claude/",{"_21":1975,"_23":1976,"_25":1977,"_108":2034,"_90":113,"_287":292,"_284":2030,"_1150":2035,"_9":2036,"_268":2037,"_20":2038,"_34":2039,"_243":2040,"_236":2041},[1981,1982,1983,1984,1985,1986,1987,1988,1989,1990,1991,1992,1993,1994,1995,1996,1997,1998,1999,2000],{"_50":23,"_54":1976,"_56":23,"_58":-7},{"_50":112,"_54":1977,"_56":25,"_58":-7},{"_50":51,"_52":289,"_54":2034,"_56":108,"_58":59},{"_50":229,"_52":1147,"_275":1148,"_62":2031,"_56":1150,"_58":-7},{"_50":51,"_52":88,"_54":89,"_56":90,"_58":91},{"_50":51,"_52":285,"_54":286,"_56":287,"_58":87},{"_50":51,"_52":282,"_54":2030,"_56":284,"_58":59},{"_50":229,"_52":274,"_275":276,"_62":2025,"_56":9,"_58":-7},{"_50":60,"_52":269,"_62":2022,"_56":268,"_58":-7},{"_50":51,"_52":266,"_54":267,"_56":268,"_58":-7},{"_50":51,"_52":264,"_54":1626,"_56":20,"_58":-7},{"_50":60,"_52":259,"_62":2018,"_56":20,"_58":-7},{"_50":51,"_52":257,"_54":258,"_56":20,"_58":-7},{"_50":60,"_52":251,"_62":2014,"_56":34,"_58":-7},{"_50":51,"_52":249,"_54":250,"_56":34,"_58":-7},{"_50":60,"_52":241,"_62":2010,"_56":243,"_58":-7},{"_50":60,"_52":234,"_62":2006,"_56":236,"_58":-7},{"_50":229,"_56":230,"_52":231,"_62":2005},{"_50":219,"_56":116,"_52":2001,"_73":2002,"_83":2003,"_34":2004,"_224":225,"_226":227,"_57":228},{"_50":51,"_56":216,"_52":217,"_54":1468},"The live first level after melee movement and a shot; ammo has fallen to 11/12.","/GameMap/media/learning/polar-icecapade-claude.webp","Polar Icecapade’s first icy 3D arena after melee propulsion and a shot, showing the moving character, gates, coins, timer and 11 of 12 ammunition.","https://evankurtzart.itch.io/polar-icecapade",[96],[2007,2008,2009],{"_52":96,"_27":97},{"_52":346,"_27":347},{"_52":1122,"_27":1123},[2011],{"_52":2012,"_27":2004,"_247":2013},"Read the team’s explicit Claude Code assistance statement","The creators distinguish AI help with diagnosing and implementing core code from their own code review, modeling, animation and art. The page links the full game source and identifies Godot 4.6 and GDScript; its “No generative AI” content badge does not erase the separate coding-assistance disclosure.",[2015],{"_52":1406,"_27":2016,"_247":2017},"https://github.com/afenkurtz/Big-Mode-Game-Jam-2026/tree/main/slick","Complete Godot 4.6 project with levels, GDScript, GLB/FBX models, Blender authoring files, textures, UI and audio. The inspected tree has 292 files, about 239 MB. Open the slick folder; importing Blender authoring files may require a compatible Blender installation. No top-level game license was found; external sounds, music and fonts retain their separately credited terms.",[2019],{"_52":2020,"_27":2004,"_247":2021},"Play or download Polar Icecapade on itch.io","Mouse recommended: left-click performs melee propulsion, right-click shoots with recoil, and Escape pauses. Browser review reached the first level, moved, fired a projectile with ammo changing from 12 to 11, and opened pause. The roughly 170 MB web build has author-documented performance limits; Windows/Linux downloads are provided and mobile is not recommended. Later levels and a complete run were not tested.",[2023],{"_52":2024,"_27":2004,"_247":-7},"Read the team’s development and asset breakdown",[2026,2027,2028,2029],"Start the first browser level with a mouse and test the slippery movement and melee combo.","Use right-click shooting and compare its backward recoil with forward melee propulsion.","Read the team’s Claude Code disclosure and human art, animation and audio credits.","Open the slick project folder in Godot 4.6, change one movement or gate rule, and test the first room, ammo and pause/restart controls.","Aidan “Botodo” Connolly and Evan Kurtz describe Claude Code helping diagnose problems and implement difficult core logic; they then touched and tweaked all code. They modeled, rigged, animated and designed the game themselves, using credited external audio. They explicitly state that generative AI was not used to create assets. No coding model version is supplied.",[1122,2032,2033],"Procreate","Affinity","Godot 4.6 · GDScript · 3D",[1122,2032,2033],[2026,2027,2028,2029],{"_52":2024,"_27":2004,"_19":302},{"_52":2020,"_27":2004,"_19":258,"_247":2021},{"_52":1406,"_27":2016,"_300":301,"_247":2017},{"_52":2012,"_27":2004,"_247":2013},[118,381,1160],"example:overexposed-ai","overexposed-ai","Overexposed","Guide a rising performer through a year of career choices in a card-based fame simulation. Play cards to build craft, money and attention while three newspapers react and excessive heat turns into scandals.","/examples/overexposed-ai/",{"_21":2043,"_23":2044,"_25":2045,"_108":2107,"_90":291,"_287":292,"_284":2104,"_9":2108,"_268":2109,"_20":2110,"_34":2111,"_243":2112,"_236":2113,"_1150":2114},[2049,2050,2051,2052,2053,2054,2055,2056,2057,2058,2059,2060,2061,2062,2063,2064,2065,2066,2067,2068,2069],{"_50":23,"_54":2044,"_56":23,"_58":-7},{"_50":112,"_54":2045,"_56":25,"_58":-7},{"_50":51,"_52":289,"_54":2107,"_56":108,"_58":59},{"_50":229,"_52":1147,"_275":1148,"_62":2105,"_56":1150,"_58":-7},{"_50":51,"_52":88,"_54":288,"_56":90,"_58":91},{"_50":51,"_52":285,"_54":286,"_56":287,"_58":87},{"_50":51,"_52":282,"_54":2104,"_56":284,"_58":59},{"_50":229,"_52":274,"_275":276,"_62":2099,"_56":9,"_58":-7},{"_50":60,"_52":269,"_62":2095,"_56":268,"_58":-7},{"_50":51,"_52":266,"_54":2094,"_56":268,"_58":-7},{"_50":51,"_52":264,"_54":1626,"_56":20,"_58":-7},{"_50":60,"_52":259,"_62":2090,"_56":20,"_58":-7},{"_50":51,"_52":257,"_54":258,"_56":20,"_58":-7},{"_50":60,"_52":251,"_62":2085,"_56":34,"_58":-7},{"_50":51,"_52":249,"_54":250,"_56":34,"_58":-7},{"_50":60,"_52":241,"_62":2081,"_56":243,"_58":-7},{"_50":60,"_52":234,"_62":2078,"_56":236,"_58":-7},{"_50":229,"_56":230,"_52":231,"_62":2077},{"_50":219,"_56":116,"_52":2073,"_73":2074,"_83":2075,"_34":2076,"_224":225,"_226":227,"_57":341},{"_50":51,"_56":335,"_52":336,"_54":1468},{"_50":60,"_56":330,"_52":331,"_62":2070},[2071],{"_52":331,"_27":2072},"https://img.itch.zone/aW1hZ2UvNTA3MzQwMi8zMTAxNTIwOS5wbmc=/original/pgaZBa.png","Creator-published gameplay screenshot from the itch.io game page.","/GameMap/media/learning/overexposed-ai.webp","Overexposed’s desktop card table with newspapers, career cards, money, fame, craft, heat and an End Turn control.","https://eg30.itch.io/overexposed",[96,415],[2079,2080],{"_52":96,"_27":97},{"_52":420,"_27":421},[2082],{"_52":2083,"_27":2076,"_247":2084},"Read the creator’s AI contribution and asset disclosure","The author names Claude Code and OpenAI Codex and explains human editing of text. README confirms AI-assisted commits with Co-Authored-By trailers; CREDITS.md explains procedural pictures/effects and the separate music/font sources.",[2086],{"_52":2087,"_27":2088,"_247":2089},"Open the complete career-simulation project","https://github.com/zsh56609/overexposed","Complete TypeScript/React project with the rule engine, content, UI drawings, procedural sound, six music files, fonts, balance simulator and browser checks. Node.js >=22.18; npm install, npm run dev or npm run build. No explicit software license is provided, so public source availability does not establish reuse rights. Bundled fonts are OFL 1.1 and Holizna music is CC0; see CREDITS.md.",[2091],{"_52":2092,"_27":2076,"_247":2093},"Play Overexposed on itch.io","Browser playtest build, best on a landscape desktop screen. Uses mouse or touch; cards show effects on hover or long press. Begin, opening text and manager choice reached the live card desk in Chrome. The complete year, all endings and touch play were not tested; the hosted build is not claimed to match the latest repository revision.","quickstart",[2096],{"_52":2097,"_27":2098,"_247":-7},"Read the game’s source and local run commands","https://github.com/zsh56609/overexposed#readme",[2100,2101,2102,2103],"Open the itch.io browser build, choose Begin and Continue, then sign with a manager.","Select an opening card offer and inspect how the desk, resources and newspapers respond.","Read the creator’s AI disclosure, README and CREDITS.md to separate code-generated art and effects from third-party music.","Use Node.js 22.18+ with npm install and npm run dev; trace content/cards.json through core/reducer.ts and the React desk before testing a complete year.","EG30 provides design, direction and writing, using Claude Code and OpenAI Codex for implementation. AI-assisted drafts of player text are edited by the creator. Art and sound effects are drawn or synthesized in code with AI assistance; the Holizna background recordings are separately credited CC0 music.",[2106],"Canvas 2D (procedural halftone art)","DOM/CSS + SVG · React UI",[2100,2101,2102,2103],{"_52":2097,"_27":2098,"_19":2094},{"_52":2092,"_27":2076,"_19":258,"_247":2093},{"_52":2087,"_27":2088,"_300":301,"_247":2089},{"_52":2083,"_27":2076,"_247":2084},[118,453],[2106],"example:katana-kitsune-godot","katana-kitsune-godot","Katana Kitsune: Prototype","Choose a kitsune fighter and face yokai in an isometric action roguelike with katana combat, stamina, pickups and successive dungeon floors. The silent prototype supports local multiplayer, with additional party systems documented in the current source.","/examples/katana-kitsune-godot/",{"_21":2116,"_23":2117,"_25":2118,"_108":2188,"_90":291,"_287":292,"_284":2182,"_1150":2189,"_9":2190,"_268":2191,"_20":2192,"_34":2193,"_243":2194,"_236":2195},[2122,2123,2124,2125,2126,2127,2128,2129,2130,2131,2132,2133,2134,2135,2136,2137,2138,2139,2140,2141,2142],{"_50":23,"_54":2117,"_56":23,"_58":-7},{"_50":112,"_54":2118,"_56":25,"_58":-7},{"_50":51,"_52":289,"_54":2188,"_56":108,"_58":59},{"_50":229,"_52":1147,"_275":1148,"_62":2183,"_56":1150,"_58":-7},{"_50":51,"_52":88,"_54":288,"_56":90,"_58":91},{"_50":51,"_52":285,"_54":286,"_56":287,"_58":87},{"_50":51,"_52":282,"_54":2182,"_56":284,"_58":59},{"_50":229,"_52":274,"_275":276,"_62":2177,"_56":9,"_58":-7},{"_50":60,"_52":269,"_62":2173,"_56":268,"_58":-7},{"_50":51,"_52":266,"_54":267,"_56":268,"_58":-7},{"_50":51,"_52":264,"_54":1626,"_56":20,"_58":-7},{"_50":60,"_52":259,"_62":2169,"_56":20,"_58":-7},{"_50":51,"_52":257,"_54":258,"_56":20,"_58":-7},{"_50":60,"_52":251,"_62":2165,"_56":34,"_58":-7},{"_50":51,"_52":249,"_54":250,"_56":34,"_58":-7},{"_50":60,"_52":241,"_62":2160,"_56":243,"_58":-7},{"_50":60,"_52":234,"_62":2152,"_56":236,"_58":-7},{"_50":229,"_56":230,"_52":231,"_62":2150},{"_50":219,"_56":116,"_52":2146,"_73":2147,"_83":2148,"_34":2149,"_224":225,"_226":227,"_57":341},{"_50":51,"_56":335,"_52":336,"_54":1468},{"_50":60,"_56":330,"_52":331,"_62":2143},[2144],{"_52":331,"_27":2145},"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/9-K9/KatanaKitsune/bc9321eeaac727bbb5372a315ec58f68c96240ac/marketing/itch/05_attack.png","Creator-published combat screenshot from the silent Godot prototype.","/GameMap/media/learning/katana-kitsune-godot.webp","The creator’s Katana Kitsune combat screenshot with an isometric courtyard, the party, enemies, health bars and minimap.","https://github.com/9-K9/KatanaKitsune/blob/bc9321eeaac727bbb5372a315ec58f68c96240ac/marketing/itch/05_attack.png",[96,2151],"GitHub Copilot",[2153,2154,2155,2156,2157],{"_52":96,"_27":97},{"_52":346,"_27":347},{"_52":488,"_27":489},{"_52":2158,"_27":2159},{"_52":1122,"_27":1123},"Meshy API","/resources/meshy/",[2161],{"_52":2162,"_27":2163,"_247":2164},"Read the creator’s AI production disclosure","https://9-k9.itch.io/katanakitsune","The author explicitly names Claude Code and GitHub Copilot alongside image, sprite and 3D asset tools, and links the primary complete source repository. The README verifies the Godot version and explains which finished assets are included.",[2166],{"_52":1406,"_27":2167,"_247":2168},"https://github.com/9-K9/KatanaKitsune","Godot 4.7 project with scenes, GDScript, Dialogic addon and finished sprite assets. The inspected tree contains about 383 MB of files; no top-level game license was found. The upstream Meshy/Blender/PixelOver authoring pipeline is separate, while its finished runtime sprites are committed. The current source contains newer party/asset changes than the reviewed hosted prototype.",[2170],{"_52":2171,"_27":2163,"_247":2172},"Play Katana Kitsune on itch.io","Silent HTML5 prototype with keyboard and gamepad support. Space confirms player/device choices; allow a clear press and release between setup steps. The browser build loaded and reached player/device selection in review; combat and a complete dungeon run were not exercised. The download is large: about 184 MB of game data plus 40 MB of WebAssembly.",[2174],{"_52":2175,"_27":2176,"_247":-7},"Read the game and asset-pipeline documentation","https://github.com/9-K9/KatanaKitsune#readme",[2178,2179,2180,2181],"Open the itch prototype and choose one human player, then claim a keyboard and select a costume.","Read the creator’s AI disclosure and the repository’s character, combat and sprite-pipeline notes.","Open project.godot in Godot 4.7 using GL Compatibility; the finished sprites and game scenes are included.","Change one combat or spawn setting, then check the title-to-character-to-dungeon flow, damage and restart.","The creator identifies Claude Code, GitHub Copilot, GPT Image 2, PixelLab and Meshy among the production tools. The repository documents Meshy rigs and animation, Blender retargeting and PixelOver sprite exports. The exact coding models and division of code between assistants are not specified; generated NPC teammates are not the evidence for AI-assisted development.",[2184,2185,2186,1122,2187],"GPT Image 2","PixelLab","Meshy","PixelOver","Godot 4.7 · GDScript · 2D / GL Compatibility",[2184,2185,2186,1122,2187],[2178,2179,2180,2181],{"_52":2175,"_27":2176,"_19":302},{"_52":2171,"_27":2163,"_19":258,"_247":2172},{"_52":1406,"_27":2167,"_300":301,"_247":2168},{"_52":2162,"_27":2163,"_247":2164},[118,381,522,2196,1160],"meshy","resource:claude-code","resource","A coding agent that reads and edits projects, runs tools, and supports skills, hooks, and MCP through terminal and IDE interfaces.","/resources/",{"_21":118,"_2262":96,"_287":2263,"_50":2264,"_2261":2199,"_2256":2255,"_27":2253,"_60":2265,"_2241":2266,"_2234":2267,"_2230":2268,"_2227":218},[2204,2205,2206,2207,2208,2209,2210,2211,2212,2213,2214,2215,2216],"website/src/data/resources.json",{"_50":23,"_54":96,"_56":2262,"_58":-7},{"_50":112,"_54":2199,"_56":2261,"_58":-7},{"_50":51,"_52":2259,"_54":2260,"_56":287,"_58":91},{"_50":51,"_52":2257,"_54":2258,"_56":50,"_58":91},{"_50":51,"_52":2254,"_54":2255,"_56":2256,"_58":59},{"_50":60,"_52":251,"_62":2251,"_56":27,"_58":-7},{"_50":60,"_52":2247,"_62":2248,"_56":60,"_58":-7},{"_50":229,"_52":2239,"_275":1148,"_62":2240,"_56":2241,"_58":-7},{"_50":229,"_52":2232,"_275":1148,"_62":2233,"_56":2234,"_58":-7},{"_50":229,"_52":2228,"_275":1148,"_62":2229,"_56":2230,"_58":-7},{"_50":51,"_52":2226,"_54":218,"_56":2227,"_58":91},{"_50":51,"_56":2223,"_52":2224,"_54":2225},{"_50":60,"_56":2217,"_52":2218,"_62":2219},"identitySource","Identity evidence",[2220],{"_52":2221,"_27":2222},"Anthropic","https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code","identity","Identity & attribution","Official Anthropic product and SDK. The organization avatar is an official corporate mark.","Source reviewed","verified","Tracks",[288,89,223